1
00:00:00,043 --> 00:00:01,044
GridBot Builder.

2
00:00:01,634 --> 00:00:02,784
GridBot Blueprint.

3
00:00:03,349 --> 00:00:04,113
Lesson two.

4
00:00:04,633 --> 00:00:06,141
What you are going to need.

5
00:00:06,952 --> 00:00:08,098
Education only.

6
00:00:08,657 --> 00:00:09,971
Not financial advice.

7
00:00:10,491 --> 00:00:12,314
This is general information

8
00:00:12,314 --> 00:00:14,746
and doesn't consider your objectives,

9
00:00:14,746 --> 00:00:16,646
financial situation or needs.

10
00:00:17,166 --> 00:00:18,930
Crypto is high risk; you could

11
00:00:18,930 --> 00:00:20,621
lose all the money you put in.

12
00:00:21,141 --> 00:00:23,192
Past performance is not a reliable

13
00:00:23,192 --> 00:00:24,890
indicator of future results.

14
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:27,349
A daily close is the last

15
00:00:27,349 --> 00:00:28,354
price of that day.

16
00:00:28,855 --> 00:00:30,911
The prices are public historical

17
00:00:30,911 --> 00:00:32,673
daily closes, marked Example.

18
00:00:33,873 --> 00:00:35,773
No order is sent from this lesson.

19
00:00:36,771 --> 00:00:39,279
Crypto is a digital coin, such as bitcoin.

20
00:00:39,799 --> 00:00:41,933
A range is the top and the bottom,

21
00:00:41,933 --> 00:00:44,314
a gap is the space between two lines,

22
00:00:44,314 --> 00:00:46,612
and the step is how wide that gap is.

23
00:00:47,132 --> 00:00:49,170
A stop is the rule for what you will

24
00:00:49,170 --> 00:00:51,063
do if the price leaves the range.

25
00:00:51,583 --> 00:00:53,482
Like a packing list before a trip,

26
00:00:53,482 --> 00:00:55,382
your page comes before any screen.

27
00:00:56,306 --> 00:00:57,814
By the end you will fill in

28
00:00:57,814 --> 00:00:59,753
a seven-item checklist on paper.

29
00:01:00,953 --> 00:01:03,244
You will keep every secret off that page.

30
00:01:04,251 --> 00:01:06,096
You will mark the page Example so

31
00:01:06,096 --> 00:01:07,828
nobody can read it as an order.

32
00:01:08,936 --> 00:01:11,100
The seven items are: a notebook,

33
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:13,524
three words, range, levels and stop,

34
00:01:13,524 --> 00:01:15,775
the pair, paper or a demo account,

35
00:01:15,775 --> 00:01:17,852
no secrets, a written stop, and

36
00:01:17,852 --> 00:01:20,189
the word Example on every figure.

37
00:01:20,709 --> 00:01:22,090
Each item has a reason.

38
00:01:22,610 --> 00:01:23,951
The notebook is the plan

39
00:01:23,951 --> 00:01:25,068
you can check later.

40
00:01:25,321 --> 00:01:26,662
The three words stop you

41
00:01:26,662 --> 00:01:28,282
drawing a grid with no edges.

42
00:01:28,651 --> 00:01:29,936
The pair names what you

43
00:01:29,936 --> 00:01:31,389
buy and what you pay with.

44
00:01:31,763 --> 00:01:33,227
Paper or a demo is learner

45
00:01:33,227 --> 00:01:34,761
plates, or training wheels.

46
00:01:35,281 --> 00:01:37,460
No secrets keeps the keys off the page.

47
00:01:37,953 --> 00:01:39,684
The written stop is the action.

48
00:01:39,977 --> 00:01:41,765
Example marks a teaching number.

49
00:01:42,176 --> 00:01:43,684
For this course the pair is

50
00:01:43,684 --> 00:01:45,323
bitcoin priced in US dollars.

51
00:01:45,843 --> 00:01:48,035
A demo account uses pretend money.

52
00:01:48,555 --> 00:01:49,974
A daily close is the last

53
00:01:49,974 --> 00:01:50,924
price of the day.

54
00:01:51,416 --> 00:01:52,869
You are naming that public

55
00:01:52,869 --> 00:01:54,433
series, not choosing an app.

56
00:01:55,245 --> 00:01:56,977
Three words, before any number.

57
00:01:57,382 --> 00:01:59,967
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

58
00:02:00,487 --> 00:02:02,511
An order is an instruction to buy

59
00:02:02,511 --> 00:02:04,460
or sell that can wait for a price.

60
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:07,347
Levels are the price lines where orders

61
00:02:07,347 --> 00:02:09,414
wait, like the rungs of a ladder, and

62
00:02:09,414 --> 00:02:11,593
a gap is the space between two of them.

63
00:02:12,026 --> 00:02:14,374
A stop is the rule for what you will do if

64
00:02:14,374 --> 00:02:16,869
a daily close finishes outside the range

65
00:02:16,869 --> 00:02:19,364
and the next daily close is still outside.

66
00:02:19,884 --> 00:02:21,705
The figures from lesson 1 are

67
00:02:21,705 --> 00:02:23,373
on the card, marked Example.

68
00:02:23,893 --> 00:02:25,569
If you can only say one of the

69
00:02:25,569 --> 00:02:27,804
three words, the page is missing a part.

70
00:02:28,674 --> 00:02:30,797
A wallet is where your crypto is held.

71
00:02:31,113 --> 00:02:33,013
A seed phrase is the list of words

72
00:02:33,013 --> 00:02:34,420
that unlocks that wallet.

73
00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:36,337
A private key is a secret

74
00:02:36,337 --> 00:02:37,803
that can move your crypto.

75
00:02:38,323 --> 00:02:41,036
An API secret is a password that lets

76
00:02:41,036 --> 00:02:43,749
a program place orders on an account,

77
00:02:43,749 --> 00:02:46,281
and sometimes move money out of it.

78
00:02:46,801 --> 00:02:49,613
You never type a seed phrase, a private

79
00:02:49,613 --> 00:02:52,153
key, or an API secret onto this page.

80
00:02:52,673 --> 00:02:54,472
The chart has no balance on it.

81
00:02:54,992 --> 00:02:56,947
A public close is not your account.

82
00:02:57,422 --> 00:02:59,053
If a form asks for a secret,

83
00:02:59,053 --> 00:03:00,839
that form is not this lesson.

84
00:03:01,889 --> 00:03:03,863
You copy the range onto the page,

85
00:03:03,863 --> 00:03:05,305
not every day's prices.

86
00:03:05,825 --> 00:03:08,059
Copy the bottom line and the top

87
00:03:08,059 --> 00:03:10,207
line, with six gaps of about 900.

88
00:03:10,727 --> 00:03:12,180
Every close in that window

89
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:13,520
stayed inside the range.

90
00:03:13,944 --> 00:03:15,346
Mark each figure Example.

91
00:03:16,396 --> 00:03:18,013
Worked check: pair, range,

92
00:03:18,013 --> 00:03:19,467
gaps, stop, and Example.

93
00:03:19,987 --> 00:03:22,202
If the stop line is only a tick with no

94
00:03:22,202 --> 00:03:24,269
sentence, the page fails the check.

95
00:03:24,789 --> 00:03:26,572
The rule has to say: if a daily

96
00:03:26,572 --> 00:03:28,744
close finishes outside the range

97
00:03:28,744 --> 00:03:30,838
and the next daily close is still

98
00:03:30,838 --> 00:03:32,622
outside, the example is over.

99
00:03:33,672 --> 00:03:35,683
A page is the notebook you can hold.

100
00:03:36,179 --> 00:03:38,140
An exchange is the app or website

101
00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:40,101
where people buy and sell crypto.

102
00:03:40,621 --> 00:03:42,129
The screen is the exchange.

103
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:44,083
Lesson 1 ended by asking

104
00:03:44,083 --> 00:03:45,377
you to bring the page.

105
00:03:45,897 --> 00:03:47,294
This lesson is that page.

106
00:03:47,809 --> 00:03:49,820
Open the notebook before any screen.

107
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:52,797
Write today's date on the first line.

108
00:03:53,147 --> 00:03:54,990
Under it, write the word Example.

109
00:03:55,374 --> 00:03:56,853
Example means a real past

110
00:03:56,853 --> 00:03:58,261
price used for practice.

111
00:03:58,781 --> 00:04:00,904
It is not an order and not a forecast.

112
00:04:02,029 --> 00:04:03,202
Write the pair first.

113
00:04:03,606 --> 00:04:05,002
The base is what you buy.

114
00:04:05,503 --> 00:04:07,235
The quote is what you pay with.

115
00:04:07,569 --> 00:04:10,760
For this course the prices are the July

116
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:13,852
to October example window, the public

117
00:04:13,852 --> 00:04:16,544
bitcoin closes from 19 July to 16

118
00:04:16,544 --> 00:04:19,137
October 2023, so you buy the base,

119
00:04:19,137 --> 00:04:21,930
bitcoin, with the quote, US dollars,

120
00:04:21,930 --> 00:04:24,622
and that row is labelled BTC/USD.

121
00:04:25,142 --> 00:04:27,154
Every other row depends on the pair.

122
00:04:27,376 --> 00:04:28,957
We price in US dollars.

123
00:04:29,477 --> 00:04:31,229
Your exchange may charge fees

124
00:04:31,229 --> 00:04:32,701
in Australian dollars, so

125
00:04:32,701 --> 00:04:34,265
keep each in its own column.

126
00:04:34,763 --> 00:04:36,939
If a fee sum is in Australian

127
00:04:36,939 --> 00:04:39,115
dollars, that sum goes on its

128
00:04:39,115 --> 00:04:41,196
own line, labelled BTC/AUD.

129
00:04:41,716 --> 00:04:43,622
Do not put a US dollar price and

130
00:04:43,622 --> 00:04:46,138
an Australian dollar fee on the same row.

131
00:04:47,188 --> 00:04:49,773
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

132
00:04:50,529 --> 00:04:55,011
In the July to October example window

133
00:04:55,508 --> 00:04:58,694
those lines are 24,930 and 30,331.

134
00:04:59,214 --> 00:05:00,611
Both figures are Example.

135
00:05:01,114 --> 00:05:03,014
Levels are the lines between them.

136
00:05:03,304 --> 00:05:05,463
Six gaps of about 900 dollars sit

137
00:05:05,463 --> 00:05:07,461
between the top and the bottom.

138
00:05:07,981 --> 00:05:09,837
Write the top and the bottom only

139
00:05:09,837 --> 00:05:11,848
after you have said what a range is.

140
00:05:12,281 --> 00:05:14,171
Then write one gap, and how you

141
00:05:14,171 --> 00:05:16,140
got it: the top minus the bottom,

142
00:05:16,140 --> 00:05:18,030
divided by the number of gaps.

143
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:20,350
The stop sentence has

144
00:05:20,350 --> 00:05:21,691
to say what you will do.

145
00:05:22,141 --> 00:05:23,948
A bot is a program that places

146
00:05:23,948 --> 00:05:26,358
and cancels the waiting orders for you.

147
00:05:26,878 --> 00:05:29,000
Two daily closes outside the range,

148
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,757
through the top or the bottom,

149
00:05:30,757 --> 00:05:32,879
and the second close still outside.

150
00:05:33,399 --> 00:05:34,963
Then you stop the bot, which

151
00:05:34,963 --> 00:05:36,551
cancels the waiting orders,

152
00:05:36,551 --> 00:05:38,451
and you follow the rule you wrote.

153
00:05:38,963 --> 00:05:40,750
Write that stop in one sentence.

154
00:05:41,712 --> 00:05:44,443
A deposit is crypto or Australian dollars

155
00:05:44,443 --> 00:05:46,940
you send into an account at an exchange.

156
00:05:47,460 --> 00:05:49,476
An exchange in Australia asks who

157
00:05:49,476 --> 00:05:51,276
you are before you can deposit.

158
00:05:51,796 --> 00:05:54,098
That check is required by Australian

159
00:05:54,098 --> 00:05:56,030
anti-money laundering law, and

160
00:05:56,030 --> 00:05:58,258
the exchange runs it, not this course.

161
00:05:58,778 --> 00:06:00,782
You only upload identification

162
00:06:00,782 --> 00:06:02,637
inside the exchange's own app.

163
00:06:03,157 --> 00:06:05,224
This course does not name an exchange

164
00:06:05,224 --> 00:06:06,789
and does not show a balance.

165
00:06:07,049 --> 00:06:09,591
Any exchange offering crypto services

166
00:06:09,591 --> 00:06:12,210
in Australia must register with AUSTRAC,

167
00:06:12,210 --> 00:06:14,830
Australia's financial crime regulator,

168
00:06:14,830 --> 00:06:17,141
as a virtual asset service provider.

169
00:06:17,661 --> 00:06:18,926
AUSTRAC keeps a public

170
00:06:18,926 --> 00:06:20,266
register you can search.

171
00:06:20,777 --> 00:06:22,956
Check that register before you sign up.

172
00:06:23,429 --> 00:06:25,719
The register says the business is listed.

173
00:06:26,146 --> 00:06:28,381
It does not say your money is protected.

174
00:06:28,660 --> 00:06:31,255
Registration is not a safety guarantee.

175
00:06:31,775 --> 00:06:33,706
ASIC is Australia's financial

176
00:06:33,706 --> 00:06:34,968
services regulator.

177
00:06:35,488 --> 00:06:38,429
From April 2027, platforms that hold

178
00:06:38,429 --> 00:06:41,272
crypto for you need an ASIC licence,

179
00:06:41,272 --> 00:06:44,213
with a transition period to October

180
00:06:44,213 --> 00:06:47,350
2027 for platforms already operating.

181
00:06:47,870 --> 00:06:49,881
Check ASIC for the current position.

182
00:06:50,128 --> 00:06:52,109
This lesson names only government

183
00:06:52,109 --> 00:06:53,561
bodies, never an exchange.

184
00:06:54,593 --> 00:06:56,269
A second code, as well as your

185
00:06:56,269 --> 00:06:58,708
password, is two-factor authentication.

186
00:06:59,228 --> 00:07:01,328
Turn that on before any real dollars.

187
00:07:01,848 --> 00:07:03,881
Then look for a paper or demo mode.

188
00:07:04,467 --> 00:07:05,989
Paper uses pretend money.

189
00:07:06,509 --> 00:07:08,129
That practice is lesson 7.

190
00:07:09,179 --> 00:07:10,687
A fill is when your waiting

191
00:07:10,687 --> 00:07:11,974
order actually trades.

192
00:07:12,494 --> 00:07:14,785
A maker fee is the charge when your order

193
00:07:14,785 --> 00:07:16,908
waits and someone else trades with it.

194
00:07:17,118 --> 00:07:18,794
A taker fee is the charge when

195
00:07:18,794 --> 00:07:20,526
your order fills straight away.

196
00:07:20,862 --> 00:07:22,560
A grid uses waiting orders,

197
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:24,259
so read the maker fee first.

198
00:07:24,779 --> 00:07:26,231
Some bots also pay a taker

199
00:07:26,231 --> 00:07:27,684
fee when they first start.

200
00:07:28,093 --> 00:07:30,915
In this example both are 0.1 percent.

201
00:07:31,435 --> 00:07:34,515
On an example buy of 100 Australian

202
00:07:34,515 --> 00:07:37,276
dollars, 0.1 percent is 10 cents.

203
00:07:37,796 --> 00:07:39,919
The sell costs about 10 cents as well.

204
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:42,084
The round trip is about 20

205
00:07:42,084 --> 00:07:44,016
cents, which is 0.2 percent.

206
00:07:44,536 --> 00:07:46,574
This fee row is Australian dollars.

207
00:07:47,094 --> 00:07:48,156
It is not the July

208
00:07:48,156 --> 00:07:49,826
to October example window.

209
00:07:50,346 --> 00:07:52,658
If the gap is smaller than that 0.2

210
00:07:52,658 --> 00:07:55,134
percent, each completed buy and sell

211
00:07:55,134 --> 00:07:57,776
costs more in fees than the gap is worth.

212
00:07:58,296 --> 00:08:00,250
To compare them, turn the gap into

213
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:02,422
a percent by dividing it by the price.

214
00:08:02,942 --> 00:08:05,939
In the lesson 1 example, 900

215
00:08:05,939 --> 00:08:09,345
divided by 27,630 is about 3.3

216
00:08:09,345 --> 00:08:12,887
percent, well above 0.2 percent.

217
00:08:13,407 --> 00:08:14,951
Lesson 5 is where you test

218
00:08:14,951 --> 00:08:16,275
a gap against this fee.

219
00:08:16,795 --> 00:08:18,862
You do not pick a gap in this lesson.

220
00:08:19,495 --> 00:08:21,381
A stablecoin is a coin built

221
00:08:21,381 --> 00:08:23,595
to stay worth about one US dollar.

222
00:08:24,115 --> 00:08:25,735
It can still lose that value.

223
00:08:26,204 --> 00:08:28,657
If your pair is priced in a stablecoin,

224
00:08:28,657 --> 00:08:31,190
every fill trades one coin for another,

225
00:08:31,190 --> 00:08:32,614
so every fill is a swap.

226
00:08:33,664 --> 00:08:35,869
A trading journal is a dated record

227
00:08:35,869 --> 00:08:37,162
of every bot: the plan,

228
00:08:37,162 --> 00:08:39,063
the changes, the fills, the fees,

229
00:08:39,063 --> 00:08:40,964
a review note of what happened,

230
00:08:40,964 --> 00:08:43,170
and whether you followed the rules.

231
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:45,477
That note is not money you made.

232
00:08:45,826 --> 00:08:47,960
A stablecoin fill goes in the journal.

233
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:50,793
The tax office treats a swap like a sale,

234
00:08:50,793 --> 00:08:52,743
so every swap goes in the journal.

235
00:08:53,263 --> 00:08:55,548
The journal is also the page you will

236
00:08:55,548 --> 00:08:57,757
open again in lesson 8 and lesson 10.

237
00:08:58,277 --> 00:09:00,802
For every transaction, including a buy,

238
00:09:00,802 --> 00:09:02,854
a sell, a swap, or a transfer, write

239
00:09:02,854 --> 00:09:05,301
the date and time, the amount, the value

240
00:09:05,301 --> 00:09:07,511
in Australian dollars at the time,

241
00:09:07,511 --> 00:09:09,957
the fee, which exchange or wallet, what

242
00:09:09,957 --> 00:09:12,246
it was for, and who the other side was.

243
00:09:12,766 --> 00:09:14,840
The columns are the date, the pair,

244
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:16,607
the range, the gaps, the money

245
00:09:16,607 --> 00:09:18,067
in the bot, the stop rule,

246
00:09:18,067 --> 00:09:20,217
the fills, the fees, the Australian

247
00:09:20,217 --> 00:09:22,368
dollar value of each fill, a review

248
00:09:22,368 --> 00:09:24,380
note, and a yes or no for the rules.

249
00:09:24,886 --> 00:09:26,523
The Australian dollar value

250
00:09:26,523 --> 00:09:28,092
column is the one exception.

251
00:09:28,612 --> 00:09:30,120
It is for your tax records.

252
00:09:30,637 --> 00:09:32,740
Download your exchange's transaction

253
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:34,752
history at least every three months.

254
00:09:35,173 --> 00:09:36,178
Keep those records

255
00:09:36,178 --> 00:09:37,519
for at least five years.

256
00:09:37,875 --> 00:09:39,647
This is general information,

257
00:09:39,647 --> 00:09:40,534
not tax advice.

258
00:09:41,054 --> 00:09:42,841
Leave two columns blank for now.

259
00:09:43,260 --> 00:09:44,424
One is for the fees.

260
00:09:44,944 --> 00:09:47,234
One is for whether you followed the rule.

261
00:09:47,368 --> 00:09:48,542
You fill those later.

262
00:09:48,991 --> 00:09:50,834
You do not fill them with a hope.

263
00:09:51,495 --> 00:09:53,885
Nobody from this course will ask

264
00:09:53,885 --> 00:09:55,833
for a seed phrase, a private

265
00:09:55,833 --> 00:09:57,250
key, or an API secret.

266
00:09:57,770 --> 00:09:59,746
If a message rushes you to send

267
00:09:59,746 --> 00:10:01,168
crypto, or asks for one

268
00:10:01,168 --> 00:10:02,828
of those, treat it as a scam.

269
00:10:03,348 --> 00:10:04,577
It is not this course.

270
00:10:05,589 --> 00:10:08,084
ASIC's Moneysmart website is the public

271
00:10:08,084 --> 00:10:10,285
Australian guide for scam warnings.

272
00:10:10,806 --> 00:10:11,811
Check it yourself.

273
00:10:12,802 --> 00:10:14,798
Now cover the chart and say your

274
00:10:14,798 --> 00:10:16,795
page out loud: the pair, the range,

275
00:10:16,795 --> 00:10:18,407
the gaps and the stop rule.

276
00:10:18,927 --> 00:10:20,928
Name the pair, the range, the gaps,

